      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 8 - Cover a song\n\nA song you already have, sung again in another style. Its tune is kept;\nthe genre, the voice and the instruments are whatever the style line says.\n**YuE2 Transcribe** writes down the recording's tune and words, and\n**YuE2 Generate Song** sings them.\n\n## What it needs\n\n- The YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB.\n- SheetSage2, 1.29 GB, which writes the tune down.\n- With **lyrics_auto_recognition** on, as here, Qwen3-ASR-1.7B, 3.8 GB,\n  which hears the words, and a language model that breaks them into lines:\n  the writer's own, 2.7 GB, when this machine has none.\n\nAll of it downloads on the first run, with progress on each node.\n\n## Before pressing Run\n\n1. **Choose the recording** on *The recording*. A song with a singer works\n   best.\n2. **Write the style** on *Sing it*. Leave the language out, or name the\n   one the song is sung in.\n3. To skip the speech model, turn **lyrics_auto_recognition** off on\n   *Hear it*, run once, and write the words under the section tags with\n   **Edit lyrics...** there.\n\n## Read the words\n\nRecognised words are close, not exact: on real songs one word in ten to\none in four came out wrong, and the wrong ones sound like the right ones.\n**Edit lyrics...** on *Hear it* shows them under their sections. Fix them\nthere and press Run again -- nothing is heard twice, because the\ntranscription and the words are kept for the recording.\n\n## Why cot is melody\n\n`melody` keeps the recording's tune and lets the accompaniment follow the\nnew style. Setting **mode** on *Hear it* and **cot** in *Settings* to `full`\ntogether keeps its chords as well.\n\n## Length\n\nAt **max_seconds** `0` the song may run 12 seconds for each sung line.\nIf the cover stops before the tune does, raise **max_seconds** in\n*Settings*.\n\n## Next\n\n**Edit score...** on *Hear it* opens the transcription on a piano roll, to\nfix a note it heard wrong. **7 - Sing a MIDI file** does the same from a\nMIDI file, with nothing to hear."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# 8 - Cover a song\n\nA song you already have, sung again in another style. Its tune is kept;\nthe genre, the voice and the instruments are whatever the style line says.\n**YuE2 Transcribe** writes down the recording's tune and words, and\n**YuE2 Generate Song** sings them.\n\n## What it needs\n\n- The YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB.\n- SheetSage2, 1.29 GB, which writes the tune down.\n- With **lyrics_auto_recognition** on, as here, Qwen3-ASR-1.7B, 3.8 GB,\n  which hears the words, and a language model that breaks them into lines:\n  the writer's own, 2.7 GB, when this machine has none.\n\nAll of it downloads on the first run, with progress on each node.\n\n## Before pressing Run\n\n1. **Choose the recording** on *The recording*. A song with a singer works\n   best.\n2. **Write the style** on *Sing it*. Leave the language out, or name the\n   one the song is sung in.\n3. To skip the speech model, turn **lyrics_auto_recognition** off on\n   *Hear it*, run once, and write the words under the section tags with\n   **Edit lyrics...** there.\n\n## Read the words\n\nRecognised words are close, not exact: on real songs one word in ten to\none in four came out wrong, and the wrong ones sound like the right ones.\n**Edit lyrics...** on *Hear it* shows them under their sections. Fix them\nthere and press Run again -- nothing is heard twice, because the\ntranscription and the words are kept for the recording.\n\n## Why cot is melody\n\n`melody` keeps the recording's tune and lets the accompaniment follow the\nnew style. Setting **mode** on *Hear it* and **cot** in *Settings* to `full`\ntogether keeps its chords as well.\n\n## Length\n\nAt **max_seconds** `0` the song may run 12 seconds for each sung line.\nIf the cover stops before the tune does, raise **max_seconds** in\n*Settings*.\n\n## Next\n\n**Edit score...** on *Hear it* opens the transcription on a piano roll, to\nfix a note it heard wrong. **7 - Sing a MIDI file** does the same from a\nMIDI file, with nothing to hear."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
